---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import servicesFaq from "../../lib/schema/schema-services-faq.json";

const services = await getCollection("services");
const sorted = services.sort((a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order);

const itemListSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "ItemList",
  "name": "Real Estate Bookkeeping Services",
  "itemListElement": sorted.map((s, i) => ({
    "@type": "ListItem",
    "position": i + 1,
    "name": s.data.title,
    "url": `https://summitledgerbooks.com/services/${s.id}/`
  }))
};
---

<Base seoTitle="Real Estate & Construction Bookkeeping Services" description="Monthly QuickBooks Online bookkeeping for rentals, property management, short-term rentals, development, and construction, plus catch-up and sync fixes.">
  <div class="container">
    <h1 class="section-heading">Real estate and construction bookkeeping services</h1>
    <p style="color: var(--color-text-muted); margin-bottom: var(--space-lg); max-width: 42rem;">I keep the books in QuickBooks Online for real estate investors, property managers, short-term rental hosts, developers, builders, and trade contractors. Every monthly plan includes reconciliations, profit by property, entity, or job, and a close by the 10th. I'm a Certified QuickBooks Online ProAdvisor (Level 2) based in Kaysville, Utah, working with clients remotely.</p>
    <p style="margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);">
      <a href="/contact/" class="btn btn-primary">Book a free call</a>
      <a href="/pricing/" style="margin-left: var(--space-md);">See pricing</a>
    </p>

    <h2 class="section-heading">Which service fits your situation</h2>
    <div class="data-table-wrap">
      <table class="data-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>If you…</th>
            <th>Start with</th>
            <th>Typical plan</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Own 1–3 rentals in one LLC</td>
            <td><a href="/services/portfolio-bookkeeping/">Rental property bookkeeping</a></td>
            <td>Starter, from $500/mo</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Own 4–10 properties or several LLCs</td>
            <td><a href="/services/portfolio-bookkeeping/">Rental property bookkeeping</a> + <a href="/services/accounts-payable-receivable/">AP/AR</a></td>
            <td>Growth, from $750/mo</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Run a property management company</td>
            <td><a href="/services/property-management-accounting/">Property management accounting</a></td>
            <td>Growth or Premium</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Host on Airbnb or VRBO</td>
            <td><a href="/services/short-term-rental-bookkeeping/">Short-term rental bookkeeping</a></td>
            <td>Premium, from $1,200/mo</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Develop or rehab properties</td>
            <td><a href="/services/development-project-tracking/">Development project tracking</a></td>
            <td>Premium</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Build, remodel, or run a trade business</td>
            <td><a href="/services/construction-bookkeeping/">Construction &amp; contractor bookkeeping</a></td>
            <td>Quoted on a free call</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Are months or years behind</td>
            <td><a href="/services/catch-up-bookkeeping/">Catch-up bookkeeping</a></td>
            <td>Flat fee, from $600</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Have AppFolio, Buildium, or Stessa that won't match QuickBooks</td>
            <td><a href="/services/systems-integration/">Systems &amp; integration</a></td>
            <td>Quoted on a free call</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2 class="section-heading" style="margin-top: var(--space-xl);">Monthly bookkeeping</h2>
    <ul class="outcome-list">
      <li><strong>Rental property bookkeeping.</strong> Income and expenses by property and entity, monthly reconciliations, and statements for the whole portfolio. <a href="/services/portfolio-bookkeeping/">Learn more</a></li>
      <li><strong>Construction &amp; contractor bookkeeping.</strong> Job costing by phase, WIP schedules, progress billing, retainage, change orders, and subcontractor 1099s. <a href="/services/construction-bookkeeping/">Learn more</a></li>
      <li><strong>Property management accounting.</strong> Management fees, owner disbursements, trust accounting, and rent roll reconciliation every month. <a href="/services/property-management-accounting/">Learn more</a></li>
      <li><strong>Short-term rental bookkeeping.</strong> Airbnb and VRBO payouts split into rent, cleaning fees, and platform fees, plus occupancy tax tracking and property-level reports. <a href="/services/short-term-rental-bookkeeping/">Learn more</a></li>
      <li><strong>Development project tracking.</strong> Hard costs, soft costs, land, and carrying costs by project, with draw schedules, construction loan reconciliation, and cost-to-complete reports. <a href="/services/development-project-tracking/">Learn more</a></li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="section-heading" style="margin-top: var(--space-xl);">Cleanup and systems projects</h2>
    <ul class="outcome-list">
      <li><strong>Catch-up bookkeeping.</strong> Months or years of backlog brought current at a flat fee: $600–$1,200 for 1–2 months, $1,500–$2,500 for 3–6 months, and from $3,000 for 6–12+ months. <a href="/services/catch-up-bookkeeping/">Learn more</a></li>
      <li><strong>Systems &amp; integration.</strong> I fix the sync between AppFolio, Buildium, or Stessa and QuickBooks, automate recurring reports, migrate data, and rebuild spreadsheets so they agree with the books. <a href="/services/systems-integration/">Learn more</a></li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="section-heading" style="margin-top: var(--space-xl);">Add-ons</h2>
    <ul class="outcome-list">
      <li><strong>Accounts payable &amp; receivable.</strong> Rent collection, vendor bills, subcontractor invoices, and maintenance costs tracked and paid on schedule. Included in Growth. <a href="/services/accounts-payable-receivable/">Learn more</a></li>
      <li><strong>Tax preparation support.</strong> Tax-ready books, Schedule E support, depreciation schedules, and entity-level P&amp;Ls, with direct answers to your CPA's questions. <a href="/services/tax-prep-support/">Learn more</a></li>
      <li><strong>Payroll support.</strong> Payroll processing, hour tracking, and payroll tax calculations, run by a QuickBooks Payroll-certified ProAdvisor. Included in Premium. <a href="/services/payroll-support/">Learn more</a></li>
      <li><strong>Financial reporting.</strong> P&amp;L by property or job, balance sheet, and cash flow statement each month, investor-ready for partners and lenders. <a href="/services/financial-reporting/">Learn more</a></li>
    </ul>

    <!-- My Process -->
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="margin-top: var(--space-xl);">My Process</h2>
    <p style="color: var(--color-text-muted); margin-bottom: var(--space-lg); max-width: 42rem;">Every client goes through the same five-step process. It keeps things consistent, thorough, and predictable every month.</p>

    <div class="process-list">
      <div class="process-item">
        <div class="process-icon">
          <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71"/>
            <path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Connect &amp; Align</h3>
          <p>I start with a call to understand your portfolio structure, entity setup, and current state of your books. I connect your accounts, configure your chart of accounts <span class="term">(the category system your books are organized by)</span> for real estate, and establish a clear baseline. Most clients are fully set up within two weeks.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="process-item">
        <div class="process-icon">
          <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path d="M9 11l3 3L22 4"/>
            <path d="M21 12v7a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h11"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Clean &amp; Organize</h3>
          <p>If your books have gaps or inconsistencies, I work through them systematically. Every transaction is categorized correctly, every account is reconciled <span class="term">(matched against your actual bank statements)</span>, and your records are brought up to date before I move forward.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="process-item">
        <div class="process-icon">
          <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="18" rx="2" ry="2"/>
            <line x1="16" y1="2" x2="16" y2="6"/>
            <line x1="8" y1="2" x2="8" y2="6"/>
            <line x1="3" y1="10" x2="21" y2="10"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Maintain Weekly</h3>
          <p>I review and categorize new transactions every week so nothing accumulates or falls behind. This keeps your books current, catches errors early, and means month-end close is never a scramble.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="process-item">
        <div class="process-icon">
          <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <line x1="18" y1="20" x2="18" y2="10"/>
            <line x1="12" y1="20" x2="12" y2="4"/>
            <line x1="6" y1="20" x2="6" y2="14"/>
            <line x1="2" y1="20" x2="22" y2="20"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Close &amp; Review</h3>
          <p>By the 10th of each month, I close the prior month's books, reconcile all accounts, and prepare your financial statements. Every line is reviewed for accuracy before anything goes out.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="process-item">
        <div class="process-icon">
          <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <polyline points="23 6 13.5 15.5 8.5 10.5 1 18"/>
            <polyline points="17 6 23 6 23 12"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Deliver &amp; Improve</h3>
          <p>I deliver your monthly reports and stay available to answer questions. Over time, I look for ways to improve categorization, refine reporting by property or entity, and give you better financial visibility across your portfolio.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- How I Work With Your CPA -->
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="margin-top: var(--space-xl);">How I Work With Your CPA</h2>
    <div class="cpa-collab">
      <ul>
        <li>I provide your CPA with clean, reconciled books organized by property and entity, so they can move quickly and accurately.</li>
        <li>I prepare supporting schedules including depreciation <span class="term">(the year-by-year tax write-off of your properties)</span>, loan amortization, and entity-level profit and loss statements.</li>
        <li>I communicate directly with your CPA during tax season to answer questions and provide any additional detail they need.</li>
        <li>I don't file your taxes. My job is to make sure your CPA has everything they need to do theirs, on time and without the back-and-forth.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- What I Don't Do -->
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="margin-top: var(--space-xl);">What I Don't Do</h2>
    <p style="color: var(--color-text-muted); margin-bottom: var(--space-lg); max-width: 42rem;">These sit outside bookkeeping, and I'll point you to the right professional.</p>
    <div class="no-services">
      <div class="no-service-item">
        <h4>
          <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/>
            <line x1="15" y1="9" x2="9" y2="15"/>
            <line x1="9" y1="9" x2="15" y2="15"/>
          </svg>
          No Tax Filing
        </h4>
        <p>I prepare your books for your CPA. I don't prepare or file tax returns. For tax filing, you need a licensed CPA or enrolled agent.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="no-service-item">
        <h4>
          <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/>
            <line x1="15" y1="9" x2="9" y2="15"/>
            <line x1="9" y1="9" x2="15" y2="15"/>
          </svg>
          No Legal Advice
        </h4>
        <p>I can't advise on entity structure, contracts, or legal matters. For questions about LLCs, partnerships, or real estate law, consult a licensed attorney.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="no-service-item">
        <h4>
          <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/>
            <line x1="15" y1="9" x2="9" y2="15"/>
            <line x1="9" y1="9" x2="15" y2="15"/>
          </svg>
          No Investment Advice
        </h4>
        <p>I track the numbers; I don't tell you what to buy, sell, or hold. For investment guidance on your real estate portfolio, consult a licensed financial advisor.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="no-service-item">
        <h4>
          <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/>
            <line x1="15" y1="9" x2="9" y2="15"/>
            <line x1="9" y1="9" x2="15" y2="15"/>
          </svg>
          No Audited or Reviewed Statements
        </h4>
        <p>If your bonding company or lender needs reviewed or audited statements, a CPA firm issues those. I'll have the books ready for them.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2 class="section-heading" style="margin-top: var(--space-xl);">Common questions about these services</h2>
    <div class="faq-static">
      {servicesFaq.mainEntity.map((item) => (
        <div>
          <h3>{item.name}</h3>
          <p>{item.acceptedAnswer.text}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>

    <div style="text-align: center; margin-top: var(--space-xl);">
      <h2 class="section-heading">Not sure which service fits?</h2>
      <p style="color: var(--color-text-muted); margin-bottom: var(--space-md);">Book a free call. Tell me what you own or build and how far behind the books are, and I'll recommend a plan and quote it.</p>
      <a href="/contact/" class="btn btn-primary">Book a free call</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <script is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(itemListSchema)} />
  <script is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(servicesFaq)} />
</Base>
